{
  "id": 339017579,
  "iid": 17878,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "FTP: Fix export objects when intermediate commands like ALLO are used",
  "description": "Only certain FTP commands (RETR, STOR, STOU, APPE, LIST, NLST, MLSD)\nhave responses sent over the data connection. PASV and PORT commands\nthat set up a data connection can be followed by other commands before\nthe command that initiates a transfer (ALLOcate, RESTart, etc.)\n\nIf the first command after a data connection is set up is not one\nof those seven that actually has a response over the data connection,\nthen replace it if one of those seven follows.\n\nAlso, export objects for STOUnique and APPEnd; these are less commonly\nused (though support for APPE is considered mandatory) but also transfer\nfiles. Continue not to export objects for directory listings.\n\nFix #20181",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-11-01T00:46:41.674Z",
